{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — for example, maximize the number of complete products that can be assembled, or minimize the total production hours used?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice (the objective function) and provides examples of that choice, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a demand limit or target number of complete products to produce, or is the only limit the workshops' capacities (i.e., produce as many complete products as the capacities allow)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding production limits (demand/target vs. capacity only), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "To make one complete product, is exactly one unit of each of the three components required (a 1:1:1 ratio), or are the component quantities per product different?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the specific ratio of components required to produce one unit of the final product."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a single component be produced by more than one workshop at the same time (e.g., Component 1 made partly in Workshop A and partly in Workshop B), or must each component be assigned to exactly one workshop?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding component assignment, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the production quantities of the components required to be whole numbers (integer units), or can they be fractional?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific constraint on the variable type (integer vs. continuous)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For each workshop, is the capacity constraint a ceiling (total hours used must not exceed the capacity, with unused hours allowed to go idle), or must the workshop use exactly all of its capacity?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the nature of the capacity constraint (ceiling vs. exact usage)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If a component is produced in more than the amount needed for the complete products (i.e., there is leftover of one component while another is short), is that leftover simply discarded, or does it carry over / count toward anything?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding how to handle leftover components."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the production rates in the table constant regardless of how many hours a workshop spends on a component, or do they change (e.g., diminishing returns or setup times) as hours increase?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding the behavior of production rates."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any minimum production requirement for any component or workshop (e.g., a workshop must produce at least some hours, or a component must be made in at least one workshop), or can any workshop or component be left at zero?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether minimum production constraints exist or if zero production is allowed."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any other constraints or costs I should account for — such as a fixed cost per workshop used, a limit on how many workshops can be active, or a maximum total number of components of any type — or are the only constraints the per-workshop hour ceilings?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of additional constraints or costs, presenting examples within that single inquiry."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "should the final number of complete products be an integer (you can only assemble whole products), even if the underlying component production can be fractional?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the integrality constraint for the final product count."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "should I assume that producing extra of one component beyond what is needed for the complete products is simply wasted (i.e., only the minimum of the three component totals determines the number of complete products)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of a specific assumption regarding how leftover components are treated."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the integrality and leftover questions are still pending internal confirmation, should I proceed by assuming that the number of complete products must be a whole number and that any leftover component beyond what is needed for those complete products is simply wasted (so the number of complete products equals the minimum of the three total component quantities)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy confirmation regarding the assumptions for integrality and leftover handling, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

